    <briefdescription>
<para>Container of numerical points equipped with an <formula id="0">$\varepsilon$</formula>-tolerance and a random weight vector used to bucket approximately equal points. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A point hashes to the integer rounding of <formula id="1">$\sum w_i x_i / \varepsilon$</formula>, so points within <computeroutput><ref refid="class_point_array_aaa9d7b196dd2c6c0e20bd902678cb773_1aaa9d7b196dd2c6c0e20bd902678cb773" kindref="member">mEpsilon</ref></computeroutput> of each other land in the same bucket and can be deduplicated. The <computeroutput><ref refid="class_point_array_a25855725f62d28b2cd2f5824462a0007_1a25855725f62d28b2cd2f5824462a0007" kindref="member">RealVector</ref></computeroutput> <computeroutput><ref refid="class_point_array_ae9da90b50d3753c811166a3bc6c05f51_1ae9da90b50d3753c811166a3bc6c05f51" kindref="member">mWeights</ref></computeroutput> either comes from the caller or is filled by the <computeroutput>(epsilon, n)</computeroutput> constructor with normalised random numbers. Used by the path-tracker to recognise coincident endpoints. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
